index a059fe2..b96d317 100644
--- a/docs/validation.md
+++ b/docs/validation.md
@@ -120,3 +120,52 @@ If even more customization is required, {func}`cattrs.transform_error` can be co
 
 Non-detailed validation can be enabled by initializing any of the converters with `detailed_validation=False`.
 In this mode, any errors during un/structuring will bubble up directly as soon as they happen.
+
+## Partial Structuring
+
+Sometimes, especially when dealing with user input, it's useful to structure as much of the payload as possible instead of failing on the first problem.
+{meth}`cattrs.BaseConverter.partial_structure` does exactly that; instead of raising, it returns a {class}`cattrs.PartialResult`.
+
+```{doctest}
+
+>>> from attrs import define
+>>> from cattrs import partial_structure
+
+>>> @define
+... class Book:
+...     title: str
+...     num_pages: int = 0
+
+>>> res = partial_structure({"title": "Dune"}, Book)
+>>> res.value
+Book(title='Dune', num_pages=0)
+```
+
+Fields absent from the payload are considered failed, and failed fields fall back to their defaults (if they have any).
+Required fields without defaults prevent any value from being produced at all, in which case `PartialResult.value` is `None`.
+The names of the fields that were structured from the payload are available under `PartialResult.structured_fields`, and the failures under `PartialResult.failed_fields` and `PartialResult.error_map`.
+The aggregate exception is available under `PartialResult.errors`, and is compatible with {func}`cattrs.transform_error` when detailed validation is enabled.
+
+Nested _attrs_ classes, dataclasses and TypedDicts are partially structured recursively.
+If a nested class can only be partially structured, its partial value is used but the parent field is still considered failed.
+Collections, like lists and dictionaries, are structured atomically - a single invalid element fails the entire field.
+
+Partial results can be fixed up using {meth}`PartialResult.refine <cattrs.PartialResult.refine>`, which merges new data into the original payload and structures again:
+
+```{doctest}
+
+>>> res = partial_structure({"num_pages": "many"}, Book)
+>>> res.value is None
+True
+
+>>> res = res.refine({"title": "Dune", "num_pages": 412})
+>>> res.value
+Book(title='Dune', num_pages=412)
+```
+
+If the converter has been initialized with `forbid_extra_keys`, extra keys make the result incomplete but do not prevent a value from being produced.
+Fields with `init=False` are ignored completely.
+
+```{versionadded} NEXT
+
+```
